# 🍋 Elumichai

**Free, offline file conversion tool for Linux** — inspired by [Tangerine for macOS](https://tangerineformac.com/), but completely free, open-source, and unlimited.

![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-orange.svg)
![Platform: Linux](https://img.shields.io/badge/Platform-Linux-blue.svg)
![Python: 3.9+](https://img.shields.io/badge/Python-3.9+-green.svg)

## Features

- **Background drag workflow** — The app starts in the tray; hold Shift while dragging for conversions or Ctrl/Super for tools
- **Tangerine-compatible format wheel** — Images, video, audio, PDF, documents, slides, spreadsheets, subtitles, and archives
- **Built-in Tools** — Compress, resize, crop, trim, merge PDFs, strip metadata, and more
- **100% Free** — No trial limits, no subscriptions, no payment ever
- **100% Offline** — All processing happens locally on your machine
- **CLI Mode** — Full command-line interface for scripting and power users
- **Batch Processing** — Convert entire folders at once

## Supported Formats

| Category | Formats |
|----------|---------|
| **Images** | JPG, PNG, WebP, HEIC, TIFF, AVIF, BMP (SVG input, PDF export) |
| **Audio** | MP3, M4A, WAV, FLAC, OGG, Opus, AIFF, WMA |
| **Video** | MP4, MOV, MKV, WebM, AVI, WMV, GIF (MP3 export) |
| **PDF** | PDF → DOCX, Pages, PPTX, XLSX, JPG, PNG, EPUB, TXT, MD |
| **Documents** | DOCX, Pages, Markdown, TXT, EPUB (RTF/RTFD/text-clipping input) |
| **Slides** | PPT/PPTX → PDF, JPG, PNG |
| **Spreadsheets** | XLSX, ODS, CSV, TSV (XLS input, PDF export) |
| **Subtitles** | SRT, VTT (TXT export) |
| **Archives** | ZIP, TAR, GZIP (RAR input) |

## Built-in Tools

| Tool | Description |
|------|-------------|
| **Any file** | Compress; edit metadata |
| **Images** | Edit photos; annotate; add a background; crop; redact; create a PDF; create a collage |
| **Video** | Trim; crop; change speed; join; save frames; split; redact |
| **Audio** | Normalize volume; create an audio visualizer; trim; convert channels; bleep |
| **PDF** | Merge PDFs; organize PDF pages |
| **Actions** | AirDrop equivalent; Float; Copy; Move; Copy Path; Terminal |

## Installation

### Quick Install (Debian 12 / Ubuntu)

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Vinoth11111/Mex-Convert
cd elumichai
chmod +x install.sh
./install.sh
```

### Manual Install

1. Install system dependencies:
```bash
sudo apt install python3 python3-pip \
    ffmpeg imagemagick pandoc libreoffice-core p7zip-full \
    qpdf ghostscript libimage-exiftool-perl
```

2. Install the app:
```bash
pip3 install -e .
```

## Usage

### GUI Mode
```bash
elumichai
```
1. Elumichai starts automatically in the system tray after installation/login.
2. Drag a file from your file manager while holding **Shift** for conversions.
3. Hold **Ctrl** or **Super/Meta** (Linux equivalents of Fn) for Tools. Alt remains available for normal file-manager dragging.
4. Release the file over a ring option. Wheel navigation makes a short sound when enabled.
5. The converted file is saved next to the original.

The global drag ring uses X11. Wayland deliberately blocks global pointer and
drag interception for security, so a desktop-specific Wayland integration is
required there.

You can also associate Elumichai with files in your file manager. The installer registers
the desktop entry with `Exec=elumichai %F`, so choosing **Open With → Elumichai** opens
the wheel without showing the main window.

### CLI Mode
```bash
# Convert a file
elumichai-cli convert photo.heic png
elumichai-cli convert video.mkv mp4 --quality 80

# Get file info
elumichai-cli info photo.jpg

# List supported formats
elumichai-cli formats
elumichai-cli formats image

# Use tools
elumichai-cli tools compress photo.jpg --quality 80
elumichai-cli tools trim video.mp4 --start 00:01:00 --end 00:02:30
elumichai-cli tools strip_metadata photo.jpg

# Batch convert
elumichai-cli batch ./photos/ webp --recursive

# Check installed dependencies
elumichai-cli check-deps
```

## Elumichai vs Tangerine

| Feature | Tangerine (macOS) | Elumichai |
|---------|-------------------|------------------|
| **Price** | ~$30 one-time | Free forever |
| **File Limit** | 20 files free trial | Unlimited |
| **Platform** | macOS only | Linux (Debian/Ubuntu) |
| **Source Code** | Closed | Open Source (MIT) |
| **CLI Support** | No | Yes |
| **Batch Convert** | Yes | Yes |
| **Offline** | Yes | Yes |
| **Formats** | 30+ | 40+ |

## Architecture

Elumichai is powered by industry-standard open-source tools:

- **FFmpeg** — Video and audio conversion/processing
- **ImageMagick** — Image conversion and manipulation
- **Pandoc** — Document format conversion
- **LibreOffice** — Office document conversion (headless)
- **p7zip** — Archive compression/extraction
- **ExifTool** — Metadata reading/writing

